Check that a library can be written to before doing the work

Reported as "Access to the path '<library>/...-SYNCED.heb.srt' is denied" repeated for every
subtitle in a library: the folder is the problem, not the subtitle, and discovering it at the end
of each job costs the whole sync to learn one fact about one directory.

All three write paths (copied sidecar, embedded sidecar, replaced original) now check the folder
first and fail with a message that names it, says the original is untouched, and includes the OS
message when there is one - "Read-only file system" and "Permission denied" need different fixes.
The check creates and removes a probe file, so nothing is left behind.

Checks: 148, ALL PASS.

Version 1.1.0.39.
